  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nUpper ridging remains firmly established over the western U.S. for\ntoday as a surface low pressure system tracks across southern \nMontana. This will lead to warm temperatures, low humidity, and \nbreezy conditions, with a Red Flag Warning in effect for locations\nsouth of the Missouri River until 8pm.\n\nAn initial shortwave looks to flatten the ridge late tonight into\ntomorrow morning with a shower or thunderstorm along the Canadian\nborder, and continues along the MT/ND Border later in the day. \nZonal flow with various shortwaves look to continue at times \nthrough the remainder of the week as a trough begins to set up \nover the Pacific Northwest. This will lead to cooler temperatures \nbut more active chances for showers and thunderstorms each day.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nLowered day 1 RH blending in ADJMAV, increased HiRes guidance for\nwinds using Fv3 and wind gusts using NBM90, as well as hand edits\nto better match with neighbors. Continued using HRRR for day 1-3 \nsmoke/haze.",
